('srd35_magic_mithral_shirt','Mithral shirt','magic_item',1100,1100,'This extremely light chain shirt is made of very fine mithral links. Speed while wearing a mithral shirt is 30 feet for Medium creatures, or 20 feet for Small. The armor has an arcane spell failure chance of 10%, a maximum Dexterity bonus of +6, and no armor check penalty. It is considered light armor and weighs 10 pounds.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_armors','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Armors","market_price":"1,100 gp","roll_result":"01–50 01–25 —","raw_table_row":["01–50","01–25","—","Mithral shirt","1,100 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_dragonhide_plate','Dragonhide plate','magic_item',3300,3300,'This suit of full plate is made of dragonhide, rather than metal, so druids can wear it. It is otherwise identical to masterwork full plate.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_armors','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Armors","market_price":"3,300 gp","roll_result":"51–80 26–45 —","raw_table_row":["51–80","26–45","—","Dragonhide plate","3,300 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_elven_chain','Elven chain','magic_item',4150,4150,'This extremely light chainmail is made of very fine mithral links. Speed while wearing elven chain is 30 feet for Medium creatures, or 20 feet for Small. The armor has an arcane spell failure chance of 20%, a maximum Dexterity bonus of +4, and an armor check penalty of –2. It is considered light armor and weighs 20 pounds.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_armors','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Armors","market_price":"4,150 gp","roll_result":"81–100 46–57 —","raw_table_row":["81–100","46–57","—","Elven chain","4,150 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_rhino_hide','Rhino hide','magic_item',5165,5165,'This +2 hide armor is made from rhinoceros hide. In addition to granting a +2 enhancement bonus to AC, it has a –1 armor check penalty and deals an additional 2d6 points of damage on any successful charge attack made by the wearer, including a mounted charge.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_armors','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Armors","market_price":"5,165 gp","roll_result":"— 58–67 —","raw_table_row":["—","58–67","—","Rhino hide","5,165 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_adamantine_breastplate','Adamantine breastplate','magic_item',10200,10200,'This nonmagical breastplate is made of adamantine, giving its wearer damage reduction of 2/–.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_armors','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Armors","market_price":"10,200 gp","roll_result":"— 68–82 01–10","raw_table_row":["—","68–82","01–10","Adamantine breastplate","10,200 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_dwarven_plate','Dwarven plate','magic_item',16500,16500,'This full plate is made of adamantine, giving its wearer damage reduction of 3/–.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_armors','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Armors","market_price":"16,500 gp","roll_result":"— 83–97 11–20","raw_table_row":["—","83–97","11–20","Dwarven plate","16,500 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_banded_mail_of_luck','Banded mail of luck','magic_item',18900,18900,'Ten 100-gp gems adorn this +3 banded mail. Once per week, the armor allows its wearer to require that an attack roll made against him be rerolled. He must take whatever consequences come from the second roll. The wearer’s player must decide whether to have the attack roll rerolled before damage is rolled.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_armors','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Armors","market_price":"18,900 gp","roll_result":"— 98–100 21–32","raw_table_row":["—","98–100","21–32","Banded mail of luck","18,900 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_celestial_armor','Celestial armor','magic_item',22400,22400,'This bright silver or gold +3 chainmail is so fine and light that it can be worn under normal clothing without betraying its presence. It has a maximum Dexterity bonus of +8, an armor check penalty of –2, and an arcane spell failure chance of 15%. It is considered light armor, weighs 20 pounds, and it allows the wearer to use fly on command (as the spell) once per day.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_armors','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Armors","market_price":"22,400 gp","roll_result":"— — 33–50","raw_table_row":["—","—","33–50","Celestial armor","22,400 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_plate_armor_of_the_deep','Plate armor of the deep','magic_item',24650,24650,'This +1 full plate is decorated with a wave and fish motif. The wearer of plate armor of the deep is treated as unarmored for purposes of Swim checks. The wearer can breathe underwater and can converse with any creature with a language that breathes water.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_armors','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Armors","market_price":"24,650 gp","roll_result":"— — 51–60","raw_table_row":["—","—","51–60","Plate armor of the deep","24,650 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_breastplate_of_command','Breastplate of command','magic_item',25400,25400,'This finely crafted +2 breastplate radiates a powerful aura of magic. When worn, the armor bestows a dignified and commanding aura upon its owner. The wearer gains a +2 competence bonus on all Charisma checks, including turning checks and Charisma-based skill checks. The wearer also gains a +2 competence bonus to his Leadership score. Friendly troops within 360 feet of the user become braver than normal. Since the effect arises in great part from the distinctiveness of the armor, the wearer cannot hide or conceal herself in any way and still have the effect function.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_armors','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Armors","market_price":"25,400 gp","roll_result":"— — 61–75","raw_table_row":["—","—","61–75","Breastplate of command","25,400 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_mithral_full_plate_of_speed','Mithral full plate of speed','magic_item',26500,26500,'As a free action, the wearer of this fine set of +1 mithral full plate can activate it, enabling her to act as though affected by a haste spell for up to 10 rounds each day. The duration of the haste effect need not be consecutive rounds.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_armors','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Armors","market_price":"26,500 gp","roll_result":"— — 76–90","raw_table_row":["—","—","76–90","Mithral full plate of speed","26,500 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_demon_armor','Demon armor','magic_item',52260,52260,'This plate armor is fashioned to make the wearer appear to be a demon. The helmet is shaped to look like a horned demon head, and its wearer looks out of the open, tooth-filled mouth. This +4 full plate allows the wearer to make claw attacks that deal 1d10 points of damage, strike as +1 weapons, and afflict the target as if she had been struck by a contagion spell (Fortitude DC 14 negates). Use of contagion requires a normal melee attack with the claws. The “claws” are built into the armor’s vambraces and gauntlets.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_armors','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Armors","market_price":"52,260 gp","roll_result":"— — 91–100","raw_table_row":["—","—","91–100","Demon armor","52,260 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_darkwood_buckler','Darkwood buckler','magic_item',205,205,'This nonmagical light wooden shield is made out of darkwood. It has no enhancement bonus, but its construction material makes it lighter than a normal wooden shield. It weighs 2-1/2 pounds and has no armor check penalty.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_shields','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Shields","market_price":"205 gp","roll_result":"01–30 01–20 —","raw_table_row":["01–30","01–20","—","Darkwood buckler","205 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_darkwood_shield','Darkwood shield','magic_item',257,257,'This nonmagical heavy wooden shield is made out of darkwood. It has no enhancement bonus, but its construction material makes it lighter than a normal wooden shield.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_shields','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Shields","market_price":"257 gp","roll_result":"31–80 21–45 —","raw_table_row":["31–80","21–45","—","Darkwood shield","257 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_mithral_heavy_shield','Mithral heavy shield','magic_item',1020,1020,'This heavy shield is made of mithral and thus is much lighter than a standard steel shield. It has a 5% arcane spell failure chance and no armor check penalty. It weighs 5 pounds.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_shields','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Shields","market_price":"1,020 gp","roll_result":"81–95 46–70 —","raw_table_row":["81–95","46–70","—","Mithral heavy shield","1,020 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_caster_s_shield','Caster’s shield','magic_item',3153,3153,'This +1 light wooden shield has a small leather strip on the back on which a spellcaster can scribe a single spell as on a scroll. A spell so scribed has only half the base raw material cost. Experience point and component costs remain the same. The strip cannot accommodate spells of higher than 3rd level. The strip is reusable.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_shields','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Shields","market_price":"3,153 gp","roll_result":"96–100 71–85 01–20","raw_table_row":["96–100","71–85","01–20","Caster’s shield","3,153 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_spined_shield','Spined shield','magic_item',5580,5580,'This +1 heavy steel shield is covered in spines. It acts as a normal spiked shield. On command up to three times per day, the shield’s wearer can fire one of the shield’s spines. A fired spine has a +1 enhancement bonus, a range increment of 120 feet, and deals 1d10 points of damage (19–20/x2). Fired spines regenerate each day.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_shields','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Shields","market_price":"5,580 gp","roll_result":"— 86–90 21–40","raw_table_row":["—","86–90","21–40","Spined shield","5,580 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_lion_s_shield','Lion’s shield','magic_item',9170,9170,'This +2 heavy steel shield is fashioned to appear to be a roaring lion’s head. Three times per day as a free action, the lion’s head can be commanded to attack (independently of the shield wearer), biting with the wielder’s base attack bonus (including multiple attacks, if the wielder has them) and dealing 2d6 points of damage. This attack is in addition to any actions performed by the wielder.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_shields','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Shields","market_price":"9,170 gp","roll_result":"— 91–95 41–60","raw_table_row":["—","91–95","41–60","Lion’s shield","9,170 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_winged_shield','Winged shield','magic_item',17257,17257,'This round heavy wooden shield has a +3 enhancement bonus. Small, feathered wings encircle the shield.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_shields','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Shields","market_price":"17,257 gp","roll_result":"— 96–100 61–90","raw_table_row":["—","96–100","61–90","Winged shield","17,257 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_absorbing_shield','Absorbing shield','magic_item',50170,50170,'This +1 heavy steel shield is flat black and seems to absorb light. Once every two days, on command, it can disintegrate an object that it touches, as the spell but requiring a melee touch attack.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_shields','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Shields","market_price":"50,170 gp","roll_result":"— — 91–100","raw_table_row":["—","—","91–100","Absorbing shield","50,170 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_sleep_arrow','Sleep arrow','magic_item',132,132,'This +1 arrow is painted white and has white fletching. If it strikes a foe so that it would normally deal damage, it instead bursts into magical energy that deals nonlethal damage (in the same amount as would be lethal damage) and forces the target to make a DC 11 Will save or fall asleep.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_weapons','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Weapons","market_price":"132 gp","roll_result":"01–15 — —","raw_table_row":["01–15","—","—","Sleep arrow","132 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_screaming_bolt','Screaming bolt','magic_item',267,267,'One of these +2 bolts screams when fired, forcing all enemies of the wielder within 20 feet of the path of the bolt to succeed on a DC 14 Will save or become shaken. This is a mind-affecting fear effect.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_weapons','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Weapons","market_price":"267 gp","roll_result":"16–25 — —","raw_table_row":["16–25","—","—","Screaming bolt","267 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_silver_dagger_masterwork','Silver dagger, masterwork','magic_item',322,322,'This masterwork alchemical silver dagger is nonmagical. As a masterwork weapon, it has a +1 enhancement bonus on attack rolls.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_weapons','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Weapons","market_price":"322 gp","roll_result":"26–45 — —","raw_table_row":["26–45","—","—","Silver dagger, masterwork","322 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_cold_iron_longsword_masterwork','Cold iron longsword, masterwork','magic_item',330,330,'Listed in Table: Specific Weapons; market price 330 gp. The specific item entry is not individually written out in this SRD table.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_weapons','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Weapons","market_price":"330 gp","roll_result":"46–65 — —","raw_table_row":["46–65","—","—","Cold iron longsword, masterwork","330 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":false}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_javelin_of_lightning','Javelin of lightning','magic_item',1500,1500,'This javelin becomes a 5d6 lightning bolt when thrown (Reflex DC 14 half ). It is consumed in the attack.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_weapons','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Weapons","market_price":"1,500 gp","roll_result":"66–75 01–09 —","raw_table_row":["66–75","01–09","—","Javelin of lightning","1,500 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_slaying_arrow','Slaying arrow','magic_item',2282,2282,'This +1 arrow is keyed to a particular type or subtype of creature. If it strikes such a creature, the target must make a DC 20 Fortitude save or die (or, in the case of unliving targets, be destroyed) instantly. Note that even creatures normally exempt from Fortitude saves (undead and constructs) are subject to this attack. When keyed to a living creature, this is a death effect (and thus death ward protects a target). To determine the type or subtype of creature the arrow is keyed to, roll on the table below.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_weapons','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Weapons","market_price":"2,282 gp","roll_result":"76–80 10–15 —","raw_table_row":["76–80","10–15","—","Slaying arrow","2,282 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_adamantine_dagger','Adamantine dagger','magic_item',3002,3002,'This nonmagical dagger is made out of adamantine. As a masterwork weapon, it has a +1 enhancement bonus on attack rolls.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_weapons','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Weapons","market_price":"3,002 gp","roll_result":"81–90 16–24 —","raw_table_row":["81–90","16–24","—","Adamantine dagger","3,002 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_adamantine_battleaxe','Adamantine battleaxe','magic_item',3010,3010,'This nonmagical axe is made out of adamantine. As a masterwork weapon, it has a +1 enhancement bonus on attack rolls.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_weapons','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Weapons","market_price":"3,010 gp","roll_result":"91–100 25–33 —","raw_table_row":["91–100","25–33","—","Adamantine battleaxe","3,010 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_slaying_arrow_greater','Slaying arrow (greater)','magic_item',4057,4057,'Listed in Table: Specific Weapons; market price 4,057 gp. The specific item entry is not individually written out in this SRD table.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_weapons','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Weapons","market_price":"4,057 gp","roll_result":"— 34–37 —","raw_table_row":["—","34–37","—","Slaying arrow (greater)","4,057 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":false}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_shatterspike','Shatterspike','magic_item',4315,4315,'Wielders without the Improved Sunder feat use Shatterspike as a +1 longsword only; wielders with the Improved Sunder feat add a +4 bonus (including the sword’s +1 enhancement bonus) to the opposed roll when attempting to strike a foe’s weapon. If successful, Shatterspike deals 1d8+4 points of damage plus the wielder’s Strength modifier to the target weapon (the target weapon’s hardness must still be overcome with each hit). Shatterspike can damage weapons with an enhancement bonus of +4 or lower.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_weapons','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Weapons","market_price":"4,315 gp","roll_result":"— 38–40 —","raw_table_row":["—","38–40","—","Shatterspike","4,315 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_dagger_of_venom','Dagger of venom','magic_item',8302,8302,'This black +1 dagger has a serrated edge. It allows the wielder to use a poison effect (as the spell, save DC 14) upon a creature struck by the blade once per day. The wielder can decide to use the power after he has struck. Doing so is a free action, but the poison effect must be invoked in the same round that the dagger strikes.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_weapons','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Weapons","market_price":"8,302 gp","roll_result":"— 41–46 —","raw_table_row":["—","41–46","—","Dagger of venom","8,302 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_trident_of_warning','Trident of warning','magic_item',10115,10115,'A weapon of this type enables its wielder to determine the location, depth, kind, and number of aquatic predators within 680 feet. A trident of warning must be grasped and pointed in order for the character using it to gain such information, and it requires 1 round to scan a hemisphere with a radius of 680 feet. The weapon is otherwise a +2 trident.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_weapons','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Weapons","market_price":"10,115 gp","roll_result":"— 47–51 —","raw_table_row":["—","47–51","—","Trident of warning","10,115 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_assassin_s_dagger','Assassin’s dagger','magic_item',10302,10302,'This wicked-looking, curved +2 dagger provides a +1 bonus to the DC of a Fortitude save forced by the death attack of an assassin.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_weapons','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Weapons","market_price":"10,302 gp","roll_result":"— 52–57 01–04","raw_table_row":["—","52–57","01–04","Assassin’s dagger","10,302 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_shifter_s_sorrow','Shifter’s sorrow','magic_item',12780,12780,'This +1/+1 two-bladed sword has blades of alchemical silver. The weapon deals an extra 2d6 points of damage against any creature with the shapechanger subtype. When a shapechanger or a creature in an alternate form (such as a druid using wild shape) is struck by the weapon, it must make a DC 15 Will save or return to its natural form.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_weapons','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Weapons","market_price":"12,780 gp","roll_result":"— 58–62 05–07","raw_table_row":["—","58–62","05–07","Shifter’s sorrow","12,780 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_trident_of_fish_command','Trident of fish command','magic_item',18650,18650,'The magical properties of this +1 trident with a 6-foot-long haft enable its wielder to charm up to 14 HD of aquatic animals (Will DC 16 negates, animals get a +5 bonus if currently under attack by the wielder or his allies), no two of which can be more than 30 feet apart. The wielder can use this effect up to three times per day. The wielder can communicate with the animals as if using a speak with animals spell. Animals making their saving throw are free of control, but they will not approach within 10 feet of the trident. The trident can be used up to three times per day.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_weapons','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Weapons","market_price":"18,650 gp","roll_result":"— 63–66 08–09","raw_table_row":["—","63–66","08–09","Trident of fish command","18,650 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_flame_tongue','Flame tongue','magic_item',20715,20715,'This is a +1 flaming burst longsword. Once per day, the sword can blast forth a fiery ray at any target within 30 feet as a ranged touch attack. The ray deals 4d6 points of fire damage on a successful hit.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_weapons','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Weapons","market_price":"20,715 gp","roll_result":"— 67–74 10–13","raw_table_row":["—","67–74","10–13","Flame tongue","20,715 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_luck_blade_0_wishes','Luck blade (0 wishes)','magic_item',22060,22060,'Listed in Table: Specific Weapons; market price 22,060 gp. The specific item entry is not individually written out in this SRD table.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_weapons','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Weapons","market_price":"22,060 gp","roll_result":"— 75–79 14–17","raw_table_row":["—","75–79","14–17","Luck blade (0 wishes)","22,060 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":false}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_sword_of_subtlety','Sword of subtlety','magic_item',22310,22310,'A +1 short sword with a thin, dull gray blade, this weapon provides a +4 bonus on its wielder’s attack and damage rolls when he is making a sneak attack with it.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_weapons','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Weapons","market_price":"22,310 gp","roll_result":"— 80–86 18–24","raw_table_row":["—","80–86","18–24","Sword of subtlety","22,310 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_sword_of_the_planes','Sword of the planes','magic_item',22315,22315,'This longsword has an enhancement bonus of +1 on the Material Plane, but on any Elemental Plane its enhancement bonus increases to +2. (The +2 enhancement bonus also applies on the Material Plane when the weapon is used against elementals.) It operates as a +3 longsword on the Astral Plane or the Ethereal Plane or when used against opponents native to either of those planes. On any other plane, or against any outsider, it functions as a +4 longsword.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_weapons','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Weapons","market_price":"22,315 gp","roll_result":"— 87–91 25–31","raw_table_row":["—","87–91","25–31","Sword of the planes","22,315 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_nine_lives_stealer','Nine lives stealer','magic_item',23057,23057,'This longsword always performs as a +2 longsword, but it also has the power to draw the life force from an opponent. It can do this nine times before the ability is lost. At that point, the sword becomes a simple +2 longsword (with a hint of evil about it). A critical hit must be dealt for the sword’s death-dealing ability to function, and this weapon has no effect on creatures not subject to critical hits. The victim is entitled to a DC 20 Fortitude save to avoid death. If the save is successful, the sword’s death-dealing ability does not function, no use of the ability is expended, and normal critical damage is determined. This sword is evil, and any good character attempting to wield it gains two negative levels. These negative levels remain as long as the sword is in hand and disappear when the sword is no longer wielded. These negative levels never result in actual level loss, but they cannot be overcome in any way (including restoration spells) while the sword is wielded.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_weapons','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Weapons","market_price":"23,057 gp","roll_result":"— 92–95 32–37","raw_table_row":["—","92–95","32–37","Nine lives stealer","23,057 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_sword_of_life_stealing','Sword of life stealing','magic_item',25715,25715,'This black iron +2 longsword bestows a negative level when it deals a critical hit. The sword wielder gains 1d6 temporary hit points each time a negative level is bestowed on another. These temporary hit points last for 24 hours. One day after being struck, subjects must make a DC 16 Fortitude save for each negative level or lose a character level.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_weapons','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Weapons","market_price":"25,715 gp","roll_result":"— 96–98 38–42","raw_table_row":["—","96–98","38–42","Sword of life stealing","25,715 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_oathbow','Oathbow','magic_item',25600,25600,'Of elven make, this white +2 composite longbow (+2 Str bonus) whispers “Swift defeat to my enemies” in Elven when nocked and pulled. Once per day, if the firer swears aloud to slay her target (a free action), the bow’s whisper becomes the low shout “Swift death to those who have wronged me.” Against such a sworn enemy, the bow has a +5 enhancement bonus, and arrows launched from it deal an additional 2d6 points of damage (and x4 on a critical hit instead of the normal x3). However, the bow is treated as only a masterwork weapon against all foes other than the sworn enemy, and the wielder takes a –1 penalty on attack rolls with any weapon other than the oathbow. These bonuses and penalties last for seven days or until the sworn enemy is slain or destroyed by the wielder of the oathbow, whichever comes first.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_weapons','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Weapons","market_price":"25,600 gp","roll_result":"— 99–100 43–46","raw_table_row":["—","99–100","43–46","Oathbow","25,600 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_mace_of_terror','Mace of terror','magic_item',38552,38552,'On command, this +2 heavy mace causes the wielder’s clothes and appearance to transform into an illusion of darkest horror such that living creatures in a 30-foot cone become panicked as if by a fear spell (Will DC 16 partial). They take a –2 morale penalty on saving throws, and they flee from the wielder. The wielder may use this ability up to three times per day.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_weapons','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Weapons","market_price":"38,552 gp","roll_result":"— — 47–51","raw_table_row":["—","—","47–51","Mace of terror","38,552 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_life_drinker','Life-drinker','magic_item',40320,40320,'This +1 greataxe is favored by undead and constructs, who do not suffer its drawback. A life-drinker bestows two negative levels on its target whenever it deals damage, just as if its target had been struck by an undead creature. One day after being struck, subjects must make a DC 16 Fortitude save for each negative level or lose a character level.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_weapons','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Weapons","market_price":"40,320 gp","roll_result":"— — 52–57","raw_table_row":["—","—","52–57","Life-drinker","40,320 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_sylvan_scimitar','Sylvan scimitar','magic_item',47315,47315,'This +3 scimitar, when used outdoors in a temperate climate, grants its wielder the use of the Cleave feat and deals an extra 1d6 points of damage.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_weapons','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Weapons","market_price":"47,315 gp","roll_result":"— — 58–62","raw_table_row":["—","—","58–62","Sylvan scimitar","47,315 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_rapier_of_puncturing','Rapier of puncturing','magic_item',50320,50320,'Three times per day, this +2 wounding rapier allows the wielder to make a touch attack with the weapon that deals 1d6 points of Constitution damage by draining blood. Creatures immune to critical hits are immune to the Constitution damage dealt by this weapon.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_weapons','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Weapons","market_price":"50,320 gp","roll_result":"— — 63–67","raw_table_row":["—","—","63–67","Rapier of puncturing","50,320 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_sun_blade','Sun blade','magic_item',50335,50335,'This sword is the size of a bastard sword. However, a sun blade is wielded as if it were a short sword with respect to weight and ease of use. (In other words, the weapon appears to all viewers to be a bastard sword, and deals bastard sword damage, but the wielder feels and reacts as if the weapon were a short sword.) Any individual able to use either a bastard sword or a short sword with proficiency is proficient in the use of a sun blade. Likewise, Weapon Focus and Weapon Specialization in short sword and bastard sword apply equally, but the benefits of those feats do not stack.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_weapons','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Weapons","market_price":"50,335 gp","roll_result":"— — 68–73","raw_table_row":["—","—","68–73","Sun blade","50,335 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_frost_brand','Frost brand','magic_item',54475,54475,'This +3 frost greatsword sheds light as a torch when the temperature drops below 0°F. At such times it cannot be concealed when drawn, nor can its light be shut off. Its wielder is protected from fire; the sword absorbs the first 10 points of fire damage each round that the wielder would otherwise take.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_weapons','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Weapons","market_price":"54,475 gp","roll_result":"— — 74–79","raw_table_row":["—","—","74–79","Frost brand","54,475 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_dwarven_thrower','Dwarven thrower','magic_item',60312,60312,'This weapon commonly functions as a +2 warhammer. In the hands of a dwarf, the warhammer gains an additional +1 enhancement bonus (for a total enhancement bonus of +3) and gains the returning special ability. It can be hurled with a 30-foot range increment. When hurled, it deals an extra 2d8 points of damage against giants or an extra 1d8 points of damage against any other target.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_weapons','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Weapons","market_price":"60,312 gp","roll_result":"— — 80–84","raw_table_row":["—","—","80–84","Dwarven thrower","60,312 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_luck_blade_1_wish','Luck blade (1 wish)','magic_item',62360,62360,'Listed in Table: Specific Weapons; market price 62,360 gp. The specific item entry is not individually written out in this SRD table.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_weapons','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Weapons","market_price":"62,360 gp","roll_result":"— — 85–91","raw_table_row":["—","—","85–91","Luck blade (1 wish)","62,360 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":false}'::jsonb),
('srd35_magic_mace_of_smiting','Mace of smiting','magic_item',75312,75312,'This +3 adamantine heavy mace has a +5 enhancement bonus against constructs, and any critical hit dealt to a construct completely destroys it (no saving throw). A critical hit dealt to an outsider deals x4 damage rather than x2.','https://github.com/olimot/srd-v3.5-md/blob/main/magic-items/magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md','specific_weapons','{"source_file":"magic-items-ii-armor-and-weapons.md","source_table":"Table: Specific Weapons","market_price":"75,312 gp","roll_result":"— — 92–95","raw_table_row":["—","—","92–95","Mace of smiting","75,312 gp"],"source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md","license":"Open Game Content / OGL 1.0a","has_full_item_description":true}'::jsonb),
